trigger: When the user types /djt-test-plan, or asks to write a manual test plan, QA steps, doer test plan, or "how do I test this change", always execute the following workflow exactly.
notes: Two stages. Stage 1 is a doer plan for the author, published as an interactive artifact (links, copy buttons, result tracking). Stage 2 is a QA plan, posted to the source of the request (usually the Jira ticket) only after the author confirms local validation. Ask if the destination is unclear. Keep scope tight to the change (exclude normal regression). Only bake in target URLs you can directly observe in the repo — otherwise ask the user which environments/URLs to target before generating scripts.